answer=According to the article, *Sailor Moon* helped redefine and expand magical-hero storytelling by combining the magical girl genre with team-based superhero action.

It says the series was “**a fusion of the popular magical girl genre and the Super Sentai series**,” and that its “**dynamic heroines and action-oriented plots**” are why it is “**widely credited with reinvigorating the magical girl genre**.” The article also notes that after its success, many similar series emerged.

So, based on the article, *Sailor Moon* contributes by:
- blending transformation-based magical girl storytelling with team superhero dynamics,
- centering strong, active heroines who fight evil,
- and influencing later magical girl and female-superhero works.
